---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const title = "zero learn: how to break into work without experience";
const description = "zero is the simulator where students do real work for real companies, get scored against the top 1% of professionals, and get recruited based on receipts. Free for students. Recruiter-paid.";
const canonical = "https://learn.joinzero.ai/";
const schemas = [
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"zero learn","url":canonical,"description":description,"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"zero","url":"https://www.joinzero.ai"}},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"zero","url":"https://www.joinzero.ai","alternateName":"joinzero","founder":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Navid Nathoo"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Nadeem Nathoo"}],"foundingDate":"2025","sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/110372181/"]}
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schemas={schemas} lastUpdated="2026-05-17">
  <span class="mono-label">ZERO · LEARN HUB</span>
  <h1>Do real work. Get recruited.</h1>
  <p>zero is the simulator where students do real work for real companies, get scored against the top 1% of professionals, and get recruited based on receipts. Free for students. Recruiters pay for access.</p>

  <div class="tldr">
    <ul>
      <li>Free for students. Recruiters pay for access to scored receipts.</li>
      <li>Tasks built around real company operations, not generic case studies.</li>
      <li>Every submission is scored against top-1% professionals, not peer averages.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p style="margin-top:var(--s-7);"><a href="https://www.joinzero.ai" class="btn btn-brand">Start your first task</a></p>

  <h2>What is the wedge between zero and the alternatives?</h2>
  <p>Forage gives you a certificate. zero gives you a receipt: a piece of work a real recruiter can evaluate against the top 1% of the industry. Companies use the receipt to decide who to interview. The certificate just sits in your LinkedIn profile.</p>

  <h2>What's in this learn hub?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/learn">Cornerstones</a>: deep answers to the questions students keep searching.</li>
    <li><a href="/how-it-works">How it works</a>: the 4-step flow from task to receipt to recruiter.</li>
    <li><a href="/for-students">For students</a>: why this beats internships, simulations, and bootcamps.</li>
    <li><a href="/for-recruiters">For recruiters</a>: how to evaluate students by receipts, not resumes.</li>
    <li><a href="/for-companies">For companies</a>: B2B talent identification at scale.</li>
    <li><a href="/vs-forage">zero vs. forage</a>, <a href="/vs-ripplematch">vs. RippleMatch</a>, <a href="/vs-handshake">vs. Handshake</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/receipts">Receipts</a>: live examples of student work.</li>
    <li><a href="/trust">Trust and methodology</a>: how scoring works.</li>
    <li><a href="/about">About</a>: the people behind zero.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-q">Is zero free for students?</div>
    <div class="faq-a">Yes. Recruiters pay for access to scored receipts. Students never do.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-q">What companies are involved?</div>
    <div class="faq-a">Tasks are built around real operations at Tesla, Shopify, Stripe, and other top hiring brands. New scenarios get added as we expand.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-q">Who scores my work?</div>
    <div class="faq-a">Top-1% practitioners in each function evaluate submissions against the bar they would apply to a junior hire. See <a href="/trust">trust and methodology</a>.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-q">How is this different from a bootcamp?</div>
    <div class="faq-a">Bootcamps teach skills. zero gives you something to show. The work itself is the credential.</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
